# Limelight_AprilTags

One vision solution that we use on the robot is called the limeleight. It as essentialy a modified
raspberry pi that has a camera and outputs data over ethernet to the roborio through the NetworkTables protocol
One thing we can use Limelights for is Apriltags, Apriltags are black-and-white checkered markers simaller to a qr code.
By knowing the actual size of the tag and knowing how many pixles we can see of the tag, we can do some trigomonitry to detrmine
our relative angle and distances to the tag. Based on this data we can get the feild relative postion of the robot
by knowing where the specific tag is on the field.
